.env
.venv/
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# SQLite: the database, WAL-mode sidecars (-wal/-shm), the legacy rollback journal, and any
# local backup suffix (mug_bot.db.pre-move.bak). *.db-journal alone predates WAL mode, so -wal
# and -shm were left untracked — which made the working tree permanently dirty on any box whose
# database lived in the checkout, and deploy/update.sh (rightly) refuses to deploy a dirty tree.
*.db
*.db-*
*.db.*
bot/state.json
bot/state.json.*
scratch/dumps/
# userscripts/ ARE tracked here, with the market-tracker wsToken scrubbed to a
# placeholder. Paste your own token locally and DON'T commit it.
# Which commit this BOX last successfully deployed. Written by deploy/update.sh
# and compared by --if-changed, so an interrupted deploy retries on the next
# cron tick instead of leaving the box quietly stuck on old code. Per-machine
# state: it describes a server, not the code.
.last-deployed
